desc:GFX G Moon [drone synth]
//tags: instrument synth drone ambient mono lfo reverb shimmer arcana
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-voice (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE MOON (card XVIII of the GFX Arcana series): the path between two towers under a pale moon - illusion,
// dreams, the tide pulled back and forth. An ambient drone synth in four mono oscillators: two that sound by
// themselves (DRONE) and two that play from MIDI (LEAD), every one with its own 12 dB low-pass, a bank of four
// LFOs that can be pointed at almost anything, and four effects fed by per-oscillator sends.
//   DRONE      two mono oscillators that play by themselves: START / STOP (in the DRONE title bar; it loads stopped,
//              and presets leave it alone), TRANSPORT (lit by default: REAPER's play / record presses START, its stop
//              presses STOP; off, the drone ignores the transport), ROOT (C..B), OCT; FOLLOW lets the last note
//              played choose the root. SWELL is how slowly the drone fades in and out (and glides to a new root).
//   LEAD       two mono oscillators played from MIDI (last-note priority): MONO (every new note restarts the
//              envelope) or LEGATO (notes played over a held one glide on without a new attack); the AMP envelope
//              (ADSR, VELOCITY), a FILTER ENVELOPE amount, GLIDE and BEND. Under the hood the lead ducks the drone
//              (a sidechain compressor: DRONE DUCK in the parameter list, 40 % by default) so it sits on top.
//   DRIVE      one per pair, before the filters (level compensated).
//   OSCILLATOR SINE, TRIANGLE, SAW or PULSE; TUNE (+/-24 st), FINE (+/-50 cents), PW; its own 12 dB low-pass
//              (CUTOFF, RESO). LINK makes the second oscillator of a pair follow the first one's filter.
//              MIX crossfades the pair, LEVEL sets the pair's level.
//   LFO 1-4    SINE, TRIANGLE, SAW, SQUARE, S&H, SMOOTH (random); RATE free or synced; DEPTH; DESTINATION
//              FINE (+/-50 cents), TUNE (+/-12 st), OCTAVE (stepped, up to +/-2 octaves - through GLIDE these
//              become slow sirens), CUTOFF (+/-4 octaves), AMP, PW, MIX; TARGET one oscillator, a pair or ALL.
//   SENDS      each oscillator: TREM (through the tremolo or not), and its sends to CHORUS, DELAY and REVERB.
//              The FX LFO moves the sends (the odd and even oscillators in opposite directions); MOVES picks
//              which sends it moves.
//   TREMOLO    SINE, TRIANGLE or SQUARE (hard); RATE free or synced; DEPTH. Only the oscillators sent to it are
//              chopped, so one can hold a steady tone while the other phases in and out against it.
//   CHORUS     a stereo chorus with three L / R options: SYNC (both sides together), SPLIT (the sides swing in
//              opposite directions: mirrored detune), DRIFT (the right side runs at its own rate). RATE, DEPTH, LEVEL.
//   DELAY      stereo ping-pong, tempo divisions; FEEDBACK, TONE, LEVEL.
//   TIDE       the ambient reverb. Five modes, each with its own X control:
//                DARK   a lower octave fed into the reverb (X = its level)
//                RISE   the reverb swells in after each new sound (X = how long the swell takes)
//                DREAM  a lush trail with vibrato (X = vibrato depth); SUSTAIN latches - press it to hold the pad,
//                       press again and it fades away at the DECAY setting
//                RAIN   low diffusion, so the reverb's taps are heard as echoes (X = diffusion)
//                LIGHT  an octave-up shimmer that builds in the tail (X = shimmer)
//              MOD waves for the trail: SINE, WARP (pitch bends mostly up, like a warped record), SINK (mostly
//              down), SQUARE (stepped up and down), RANDOM. DECAY, FILTER, MOD depth and RATE, WIDTH, LO-FI
//              (sample-rate reduction of the trail), LEVEL. SUSTAIN (held): the trail grows to its longest while
//              held and falls back when let go.
//   MASTER     DRY, FATE, VOLUME, SAT (the output soft clip is always on)
// FATE (the Arcana series drift, 0-100 %, 50 % = the standard amount): the tides - every LFO's rate, depth and
//   phase wander slowly, and so do the tremolo, chorus and FX LFO rates; and each oscillator's tuning wanders on
//   its own, so the pairs beat and phase against each other.
// MIDI: pitch bend (BEND range, LEAD pair), CC1 mod wheel (adds to LFO 1 depth), CC64 sustain, CC120 / CC123 all
//   notes off.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc

